# The Level mode's zoomable tileset views (tile_zoom.odin): the tile palette and the tabs' tile
# pickers zoom like the canvas (the wheel around the pointer), pan (a middle drag; Space + drag),
# have − / + / Fit buttons, pick the tile under the pointer at any zoom and pan, and keep their zoom
# per tileset (the palette's and the pickers' apart), across layers and when the project opens again.
# Run with: task test:ui (and test:ui:fullscreen, test:ui:short)
#
# The fixture tests/fixtures/ldtk_paint/paint.ldtk (make_paint.py): its tileset Tiles (uid 10,
# 128 x 64, 16 px tiles: 8 x 4) on the Decor layer (Tiles, the Layers row 2).

wait 5
key ctrl+alt+2
expect mode Level
import tests/fixtures/ldtk_paint/paint.ldtk
expect level file assets/paint/paint.ldtk
wait_until level levels 2
wait_until widget_visible ldtk-map-Level true
double_click_widget level-row-0
expect level focus Room
wait 5
send Level_Layer_Picked 2
expect level layer Decor
wait_until widget_visible level-palette-tiles true

# Fitted: a click picks the tile under it
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles fit
click_tileset_tile level-palette-tiles 9
expect level tiles [9]

# The wheel zooms around the pointer (the view's middle here); a pick at that zoom
wheel_widget level-palette-tiles 3
wait 3
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed
click_tileset_tile level-palette-tiles 11
expect level tiles [11]
# A middle drag pans; the pointer grabs; a pick after it
drag_widget level-palette-tiles 0.5 0.5 0.3 0.5 middle
wait 3
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed
click_tileset_tile level-palette-tiles 12
expect level tiles [12]

# Fit, then +, then − (the buttons beside the palette's toggles)
click_widget level-palette-tiles-fit
wait 3
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles fit
click_tileset_tile level-palette-tiles 0
expect level tiles [0]
click_widget level-palette-tiles-zoom-in
wait 3
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed
click_widget level-palette-tiles-zoom-in
wait 3
click_widget level-palette-tiles-zoom-out
wait 3
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed
click_tileset_tile level-palette-tiles 11
expect level tiles [11]

# Remembered across layers: an IntGrid layer's palette, then Decor again
send Level_Layer_Picked 3
expect level layer Ground
wait 3
send Level_Layer_Picked 2
wait_until widget_visible level-palette-tiles true
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed

# The Tilesets tab's picker keeps its own zoom: fitted, zoomed by the wheel, Fit again
send Bottom_Tab Tilesets
wait 3
scroll_into_view ldtk-tab-scroll ldtk-picker-tileset
expect tile_zoom ldtk-picker-tileset fit
wheel_widget ldtk-picker-tileset 2
wait 3
expect tile_zoom ldtk-picker-tileset zoomed
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed
scroll_into_view ldtk-tab-scroll ldtk-picker-tileset-fit
click_widget ldtk-picker-tileset-fit
wait 3
expect tile_zoom ldtk-picker-tileset fit
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed

# Kept with the project: opened again, the palette's zoom is still there
key ctrl+s
open_project {project}
expect mode Level
wait 5
send Level_Layer_Picked 2
wait_until widget_visible level-palette-tiles true
expect tile_zoom level-palette-tiles zoomed
click_tileset_tile level-palette-tiles 11
expect level tiles [11]
